  "semantics": [
    "Open with O_NONBLOCK before checking descriptor kind so a FIFO cannot stall a blocking read-only open.",
    "Reject nonregular opened descriptors and negative/over64MiB declared lengths before reads or allocation.",
    "Read only from the admitted descriptor, compare device/inode/size/mtime/ctime around the read, require exact observed length and hash those bytes.",
    "All successfully opened descriptors are closed in finally, including fstat/read/allocation/hash failures.",
    "Missing or unusable O_NONBLOCK is explicitly refused before any artifact open.",
    "These are same-descriptor consistency checks; they do not lock pathname replacement or provide signed compiler attestation. Later parent artifact identity checks still reject substituted output paths."
  ]
